# Running the project locally

- When you need to run, debug, or test the project, bring it up with exactly this command from the project root:

  ```
  docker compose up -d --build
  ```

- The app is served at `http://localhost:8080` (see `docker-compose.yml`, `"8080:8080"`). Use that address to check it.
- Do not invent another way to run it (no `php artisan serve`, no `npx serve`, no other port, no ad-hoc dev server). If the normal command does not work, report the error to the user instead of starting a different setup.
- Do not change the port mapping to get around a conflict. If port 8080 is busy, tell the user.
